.TH ACRIMONIOUS-READER 1 "October 2026" "acrimonious-reader 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
acrimonious-reader \- PDF viewer for GNOME that can fill in and sign forms
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acrimonious-reader
[\fIOPTION\fR...] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acrimonious-reader
shows PDF documents. Each \fIFILE\fR (a path or a URI) opens in its own window; a file that is
already open is brought to the front.
.PP
Pages are rendered on a background thread, so scrolling and zooming stay smooth. The viewer has
page thumbnails, the document outline, search, links with back and forward, text selection,
night mode and printing, and it reloads a document automatically when the file changes.
.PP
Press Ctrl+E to write and draw: add text boxes, draw freehand with the pen, and erase. Ctrl+S
saves them into the PDF as standard annotations, so other PDF viewers show them too. Press Ctrl+?
for all keyboard shortcuts.
.PP
The signature button keeps signatures you draw once, so you can place them on any document with a
click. Right-clicking a drawing on a page offers to save it as a signature.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the GTK and application options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/acrimonious-reader/state.json
Where each document was left, and the window and display preferences.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/acrimonious-reader/signatures.json
Saved signatures, readable only by you.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/boergens/acrimonious-reader
